msgstr ""

#: ../../source/03-profiles.rst:12 43c2b802f2b7407baf64e7364d684a39
msgid ""
"**A profile is a quality-preserving recipe.** It fixes the codec and "
"rate-control; resolution, frame rate, and pixel format never change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/03-profiles.rst:14 721c3aa48e77474eb309bea53766d852
msgid ""
"**Lower number, higher quality.** :term:`CRF` (x265/AV1) and "
"``global_quality`` (QSV) / ``cq`` (NVENC) all run *backwards* — a lower "
"value means better quality and a bigger file. The numbers are **not** "
"comparable across codecs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/03-profiles.rst:18 ca10463e950749f8a0929ee9b7a7a8cc
msgid ""
"**Audio is normalized.** Every profile re-encodes audio to AAC 128k — "
"transparent for speech; raise it for music with ``--audio-kbps``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/03-profiles.rst:20 39a3ef8764e54bb18b1bacdda6225007
msgid ""
"**Hardware profiles trade a little size for a lot of speed.** ``qsv`` and"
" ``nvenc`` are ~2× faster and run on otherwise-idle silicon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/03-profiles.rst:23 054e9f4177d340e39671808876fbaf16
msgid ""
"Pick a profile with :doc:`benchmark <02-commands>` on your own footage "
"rather than from the table alone; the catalog below is the starting "
"point. The profile data lives in :mod:`slimv.profiles`."
msgstr ""

